 "verdict": "X186's NUMBER DOES NOT SURVIVE COUNTING WORLDS, AND THE EFFECT IS INSIDE ITS OWN BAR. The observational pool holds 742 runs, 311 of them in mixed cells, and those form 258 worlds (cell times phase): 1.205 runs per world, so about a fifth of the mixed rows are repeats. X186's deviance drop is 20.7 over runs and 14.3 over worlds (424.0 -> 403.3 and 352.9 -> 338.6), a fall of 30.9 per cent; the phase-clustered bootstrap puts the drop above X186's own bar of 20 in 0.208 of resamples against 0.517 for the run bootstrap. So the repetition is not cosmetic: with worlds as the unit, the typical resampled drop is 13.149999999999999 and more often than not below 20, which is the bar X186 used to call the local inflow better than the nominal F. The pool also differs from X186's own run (424.0 -> 403.3 against the published 464.5 -> 436.5, drop 28.0), because later arms and the selected pools are excluded here; the like-for-like comparison is the pair of this item's own readings, runs against worlds. X186's conclusion therefore needs the world as its unit in the manuscript, and X194's 'the published intervals stand' is restricted to the AUC it measured and does not extend to this deviance."
}
